The '''Andor household'''<ref name="Thisweek">{{ThisWeek|kBQJ4kGNEeY|Tales of the Jedi Arrives, Fiona Shaw Talks Andor, and More!|sw_url=video/tales-of-the-jedi-arrives-fiona-shaw-talks-andor-and-more}}</ref> was a residence where the [[Andor family]] on the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]]. By [[18 BBY]], it was home to [[Clem Andor]], [[Maarva Carassi Andor|Maarva Andor]], and their adoptive son [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]].<ref name="RR">{{Andor|Rix Road (episode)}}</ref> It continued to house Maarva, Cassian, and their droid [[B2EMO]]<ref name="Reckoning" /> by [[5 BBY]].<ref name="Kassa">{{Andor|Kassa (episode)}}</ref> After Cassian became a target of the [[Consolidated Holdings of Preox-Morlana Corporation|Preox-Morlana]], several officers led by [[Syril Karn]] invaded the home, ransacking Cassian's room and holding Maarva and B2EMO prisoner for some time.<ref name="Reckoning" />

{{Struct-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|My character's house is built from parts of old spaceships. I used to go out and just stare at it. Breathtaking.|Fiona Shaw|<ref name="Old School">{{WebCite|url=https://www.empireonline.com/tv/news/star-wars-andor-doesnt-use-volume-says-tony-gilroy-exclusive|text=Andor Doesn't Use Star Wars' Volume Video Wall: ‘We're Old-School,' Says Tony Gilroy – Exclusive Image|author=Travis, Ben|date=2022-08-01|work=[[Wikipedia:Empire (magazine)|''Empire'']]|archivedate=20220801153835}}</ref>}}
The Andor household was first pictured in the teaser trailer for the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' television series, which was released on [[May 26]], [[2022]].<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|j5UX1Adanis|Andor &#124; Teaser Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/andor-teaser-trailer}}</ref> It first appeared in "[[That Would Be Me]]," the second episode of the series,<ref name="That Would Be Me" /> which aired on [[September 21]], 2022.<ref name="Airdate">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-08-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref> It was first identified in an episode of ''[[This Week! in Star Wars]].<ref name="Thisweek" />

[[File:AndorhouseholdConceptArt.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Concept art of Cassian Andor, Maarva Andor, and B2EMO in the Andor household by Luke Hull]]
Production designer [[Luke Hull]] created a sketch of Cassian Andor, Maarva Andor, and B2EMO in the household.<ref name="Period drama">{{Getty|url=thewaltdisneystudios/allaccess#!asset/gppr5wpqgb4t74974f8s|text=ANDOR Production Brief V3 FINAL 8-04-22|author=[[Gina McIntyre|McIntyre, Gina]]|date=2022-08-04}}</ref> The household's interior and exterior were the same set, making it fully three-dimensional.<ref name="Career Highlight">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-features/andor-episode-8-toby-haynes-forest-whitaker-stellan-skarsgard-1235250954|date=2022-10-28|text=‘Andor' Director Toby Haynes Talks That Forest Whitaker-Stellan Skarsgard Scene: "It Was a Career Highlight"|archivedate=20250221213707}}</ref> The household was carefully crafted to explain Maarva's character and show that her life had become her chair. Hull worked on the chair, B2EMO's charging unit, and the hydroponics in the window.<ref name="Period drama" /> The household was made to look like it was built from parts of old [[starship]]s.<ref name="Old School" /> According to<ref name="Good day">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-features/andor-season-2-post-credits-scene-tony-gilroy-1235268962|text=‘Andor' Creator Tony Gilroy Talks Luthen's Good Day, That Post-Credit Scene and Season Two |author=Davids, Brian|date=2022-11-23|work=[[Wikipedia:The Hollywood Reporter|''The Hollywood Reporter'']]|archivedate=20221123185515}}</ref> executive producer<ref name="Kassa" /> [[Tony Gilroy]], everything on Ferrix was filmed first.<ref name="Good day" /> One of the first scenes filmed with [[Diego Luna]] and [[Fiona Shaw]], the actors who played Cassian and Maarva Andor, respectively, was an argument between the characters in the house.<ref name="Daughter">{{SW|url=news/fiona-shaw-andor-interview|text=Daughter of Ferrix: <i>Andor</i>'s Fiona Shaw on the Role of Cassian's Mother, Maarva}}</ref> Around the end of his three week stint on season one, actor [[Eugene Lin]] and his fellow performers had a chance to walk around the Ferrix village set, which enabled him to relax within Maarva's home.<ref name="Insta11-29">{{Instagram|username=its_eugene_lin|url=p/ClionQiICff|name=[[Eugene Lin]]|date=2022-11-22|quote=Behind the scenes and a frame from LucasFilm / Disney+’s  ‘Star Wars: Andor’ (2022) season 1, episode 12 ‘Rix Road’, playing an Imperial Officer (Ferrix). Despite being the season finale, the episode was actually filmed in the middle of the production run and was the last scene shot at the specially built set in Marlow. I was very excited to get into armour and was a little disappointed when we only got into the under layers, but it was also the only time I got to wear the Imperial cap. This scene involved setting up base at the hotel on Ferrix. It was a lot of fun looking at all the incredibly detailed props and getting to play with actual retractable metal batons. Toward the end of our three-week stint, we were given the thrilling privilege of roaming the entire village set for a few hours, visiting workshops, bars, restaurant and even relaxing in Maarva Andor’s apartment. Most days, I had to pinch myself because it was such a dream come true.  © 2022 & TM Lucasfilm Ltd #actionactor #behindthescenes #onset #starwars #starwarsandor #andorseason1 #imperialofficerferrix #theempire #imperialtrooper #imperialarmy #costumearmour #asianmalemodel #asianmuscle #londonmodel #singaporemodel #eugenelin|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/1AA0Z}}</ref>

